title: 'pallet-revive: remove migration v1'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Removes the multi-block migration `pallet_revive::migrations::v1`, which moved
    `ContractInfoOf` into `AccountInfoOf`, together with its weight function
    `WeightInfo::v1_migration_step` and the `v1_migration_step` benchmark.

    Migration v1 reads and writes `AccountInfoOf` through the pallet's live storage and value
    declarations, so it changes meaning whenever those types change. Making it self-contained,
    as the other migrations will be, is a larger change for v1 than for the rest, and no runtime
    in this repository or in the fellowship runtimes lists it any more, so it is removed instead.

    Required changes, in this order:

    1. Check that migration v1 has completed on the chain: the pallet's `ContractInfoOf` storage
       prefix holds no keys. The prefix is `twox_128` of the pallet's name in the runtime followed
       by `twox_128("ContractInfoOf")`. For a pallet named `Revive` it is
       `0x735f040a5d490f1107ad9c56f5ca00d2060e99e5378e562537cf3bc983e17b91`. This release has no
       code that moves remaining `ContractInfoOf` entries.
    2. Remove `pallet_revive::migrations::v1::Migration<Runtime>` from the
       `pallet_migrations::Config::Migrations` tuple if it is still listed.
    3. Delete `v1_migration_step` from your own `pallet_revive::WeightInfo` implementation, for
       example a generated `weights/pallet_revive.rs`. The trait no longer has this method, so the
       implementation does not compile until it is removed.

    Runtimes that use neither `v1_migration_step` nor `migrations::v1` need no code change.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
